 i  don't like  oils and butters and sauces  but you guys are always so accommodating  and always  cook the food exactly how i like it very  simple  very clean  incredibly fresh  and just perfect and then you know i  love some steamed vegetables on the side  some balsamic vinegar and then to season  myself so there's no denying that we all  have our food preferences and being a  fussy eater isn't necessarily disordered  but having rigid rules around how food  is prepared is one of the common traits  of an ed especially if those rules  result in the lowest calorie meals  possible it really comes down to  intention and when the quest for  simplicity and eating clean becomes an  obsession and all-consuming it often  teeters into orthorexic territory folks  with orthorexic tendencies often have a  lot of anxiety around how food is cooked  they often choose locale cooking methods  like steaming or grilling over sauteing  frying or roasting in oil they may avoid  oils butters and sauces with unknown  ingredients and they may choose low  calorie sugar-free clean seasonings like  himalayan sea salt hot sauce or vinegars  all of these rules often are used to  maintain a sense of control but long  term they actually have the opposite  effect now some may say that these are  just a preference but celebrities like  victoria have a lot of power and  influence over young impressionable  girls around the world not to mention  the dangerous message that this  communicates to her own children  obviously victoria is a very beautiful  woman and is married to arguably the  most beautiful man in the world  and i do worry that her fans will try to  mimic her preferences to yield similar  life or body results so to most  restaurants i'm probably the worst  nightmare it's not good speaking of  renowned restaurants celebrity chef  wolfgang puck has also confirmed  victoria's restrictive dining habits and  revealed that the spice girl only orders  spinach or steamed veggies with like a  little touch of salt in there whenever  her and her hubby are dining at his  restaurants that is just sad i mean i  have met and worked with wolfgang  himself and he is such a kind and  talented chef no protein no carbs no fat  not even enough calories for a snack it  is so surprising and sad and  disappointed to me that these  restrictive behaviors have been  maintained for so long without any kind  of intervention or personal attempt to  change  so i just decided from that point to  really try and eat in a clean way lots  of fresh vegetables lots of fish i don't  have any dairy at all  i haven't eaten  red meat since i was about seven years  old i eat lots of  fish and i have a very very healthy way  of eating while the quest to eat cleaner  or healthier can often be used to  moralize food and justify rigid  restrictions eating healthy foods is not  inherently disordered if it's  accompanied by an ability to be flexible  and not let these preferences control  your life there's obviously lots of  nutritional benefits to be had in meals  like this so you know we've got  antioxidants and fiber from the veggies  we got high quality protein omega-3 fats  and iron in the fish even from a  nutrition perspective we can also have  too much of a good thing just take the  mercury in fish for a minute i mean sure  some fish are lower in mercury so like  salmon and haddock for example but when  you only eat a handful of foods like  this it's still very possible to exceed  safe mercury levels so for example  eating three servings of salmon or two  servings of haddock in a day would  likely increase victoria's mercury  intake beyond what is considered safe so  this is one of the many reasons why  variety is the spice of life likewise  too much fiber from vegetables can also  result in digestive distress like  bloating constipation and diarrhea  especially if the fiber is coming from  high fodmap vegetables which can be more  difficult for some folks to digest and  the lack of diet v